{% extends 'layouts/example-synth.njk' %}

{% block audio %}
<chain-blam id="bus">
  <reverb-blam mix="0.2">
    <sample-blam src="{{site.basedir}}/static/sounds/IRs/plate.mp3"></sample-blam>
  </reverb-blam>
  <limiter-blam></limiter-blam>
  <analyser-blam id="analyser"></analyser-blam>
</chain-blam>

<synth-blam class="steel" notes="C4 D4 E4 G4 A4 C5 D5 E5 G5 A5" out="bus">
  <carrier-blam curve="0 0, 1 0.03, 0 2">
    <modulator-blam curve="0 0, 1 0.03, 0 1.25" ratio="3" gain="750">
      <blam-blam prop="gain" value="100~2000"></blam-blam>
    </modulator-blam>
  </carrier-blam>
  <carrier-blam curve="0 0, 1 0.02, 0 0.06" release="2" offset="-12">
  </carrier-blam>
  <envelope-blam prop="detune" curve="0 0, -40 0.25, 0 0.7"></envelope-blam>
</synth-blam>

<tap-blam to=".steel" prop="play">
  <button>hit steel drum</button>
  <blam-blam to="rings-blam" prop="start" once></blam-blam>
</tap-blam>
{% endblock %}

{% block dialog %}

{% renderTemplate "md" %}

A more subtle application of FM (frequency modulation) than found in the [”In A Bad Moog”](/examples/03-in-a-bad-moog) example’s “instability” control. 

In this case, the ratio is 3:1 (`ratio="3"`), creating a stable metallic timbre. The `<modulator-blam>` has a shorter `curve` than its parent `<carrier-blam>`, meaning the metallic timbre is only at the start of the sound. The effect is a pseudo-steel drum sound.

```html
<synth-blam class="steel" notes="C4 D4 E4 G4 A4 C5 D5 E5 G5 A5" out="bus">
  <carrier-blam curve="0 0, 1 0.03, 0 2">
    <modulator-blam curve="0 0, 1 0.03, 0 1.25" ratio="2" gain="500">
      <blam-blam prop="gain" value="100~2000"></blam-blam>
    </modulator-blam>
  </carrier-blam>
  <carrier-blam curve="0 0, 1 0.02, 0 0.06" release="2" offset="-12">
  </carrier-blam>
  <envelope-blam prop="detune" curve="0 0, -35 0.25, 0 0.7"></envelope-blam>
</synth-blam>
```

The `<blam-blam>` element fluctuates the `<modulator-blam>` element’s gain, simulating softer versus harder hits of the drum. The second `<carrier-blam>` emits a very short, detuned knocking sound and the `<envelope-blam>`, affecting `detune`, creates a slight bowing effect for added authenticity.

Consult the [**Synthesis guide**](/guides/synthesis) for more context.

{% endrenderTemplate %}

